'''Distribució Automobilística de Balboa, S.A.''' (DAB) is a Balboan automotive dealership group operating a network of dealerships across [[Balboa]]. The company holds franchise agreements for several imported vehicle brands, operating 11 dealership locations across the country's five provinces. It is listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] under the ticker DAB and is a constituent of the [[SCX 100]] index.

DAB was founded in 1995 by Lluís Geli i Abellà, a former sales manager at a Volisanian vehicle importer, who consolidated several independent dealerships into a single group. The company initially held franchises for [[Sparc]] and [[CdV]] vehicles in the Sant Cristòfor area, and expanded into the interior provinces through acquisitions in the late 1990s and 2000s.

The company's dealership network is concentrated in urban centres, with four locations in [[Sant Cristòfor]], three in [[Sant Bart]], two in [[Novara]], and one each in [[Portblanc]] and [[Sant Llàtzer]]. DAB holds franchises for:

* [[Sparc]] and [[CdV]] — Volisanian conventional and early EV models; Estret and Jala focus
* [[BYD Auto|BYD]] — Varkan electric and plug-in hybrid vehicles; nationwide
* [[Yonezawa Motors|Yonezawa]] — Okaiken passenger vehicles; Estret and Jala focus
* [[Vidal]] — Baliscan electric vehicles; nationwide, strongest in Estret
* [[SKQ]] — Burawi electric vehicles; nationwide, strongest in interior provinces

DAB's revenue is split approximately 55 per cent new vehicle sales, 30 per cent used vehicle sales, and 15 per cent servicing and parts. The company's used vehicle division is particularly significant in the interior provinces, where it handles trade-ins and resale of vehicles that have been replaced by newer models in the Estret market.

The company's thin margins on new vehicle sales — typical of dealership operations — are supplemented by financing arrangements, insurance products, and servicing contracts. The shift toward electric vehicles has reduced servicing revenue per vehicle, as EVs require less routine maintenance, but has increased parts revenue for battery-related components.

